{"title":"Career Roadmap · Product Engineer","role":"Product Engineer","summary":"A Product Engineer designs, develops, tests, deploys and continuously improves software products. Unlike a role focused only on implementing assigned features, a Product Engineer typically works across the full software product lifecycle and connects engineering decisions with user needs, product requirements, reliability, performance and business objectives.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Software Product Engineering (Industry-integrated)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Product Engineer designs, develops, tests, deploys and continuously improves software products. Unlike a role focused only on implementing assigned features, a Product Engineer typically works across the full software product lifecycle and connects engineering decisions with user needs, product requirements, reliability, performance and business objectives."},{"type":"p","text":"An industry-integrated program should be used to build both strong engineering fundamentals and real product-development experience."},{"type":"p","text":"A strong Product Engineer should be capable of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Translating product requirements into technical solutions"},{"text":"Designing software architecture"},{"text":"Building frontend and backend systems"},{"text":"Designing APIs and databases"},{"text":"Writing production-quality code"},{"text":"Testing and debugging"},{"text":"Deploying applications"},{"text":"Monitoring production systems"},{"text":"Understanding user behavior and product metrics"},{"text":"Collaborating with product, design and business teams"},{"text":"Iterating based on feedback"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Core Career Positioning"},{"type":"flow","items":["Computer Science Fundamentals","Full-Stack Engineering","System Design","Cloud","DevOps","Product Thinking","Testing","Observability","AI-assisted Development"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech / B.E. Software Product Engineering","Programming + CS Fundamentals","Data Structures + Algorithms","Software Engineering Practices","Frontend + Backend + Database Development","API + System Design","Testing + Security + Git/CI-CD","Cloud + Containers + DevOps","Product Analytics + User-Centric Development","Industry Project / Internship","Product Engineer Trainee","Product Engineer","Senior Product Engineer","Staff / Lead Product Engineer","Principal Engineer / Architect"]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career Stage","Typical Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Student"},{"text":"Programming, CS fundamentals, projects"}],[{"text":"Intern"},{"text":"Feature development and engineering workflows"}],[{"text":"Trainee"},{"text":"Production code and team practices"}],[{"text":"Product Engineer"},{"text":"End-to-end feature/product ownership"}],[{"text":"Senior Product Engineer"},{"text":"Architecture, reliability, mentoring"}],[{"text":"Lead/Staff Engineer"},{"text":"Technical direction and system design"}],[{"text":"Principal Engineer"},{"text":"Organization-wide technical strategy"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During B.Tech / B.E.","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Programming & Computer Science Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Start with one primary programming language."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended"},{"type":"p","text":"Java or C++ for strong engineering fundamentals."},{"type":"p","text":"Also learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python"},{"text":"JavaScript / TypeScript"},{"text":"Git"},{"text":"Linux fundamentals"},{"text":"Command line"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Programming Concepts"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Variables"},{"text":"Data types"},{"text":"Functions"},{"text":"OOP"},{"text":"Exception handling"},{"text":"Collections"},{"text":"File handling"},{"text":"Generics"},{"text":"Basic concurrency"},{"text":"Debugging"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data Structures & Algorithms"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a strong DSA foundation."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Arrays"},{"text":"Strings"},{"text":"Linked lists"},{"text":"Stacks"},{"text":"Queues"},{"text":"Hashing"},{"text":"Trees"},{"text":"Binary search trees"},{"text":"Heaps"},{"text":"Graphs"},{"text":"Tries"},{"text":"Recursion"},{"text":"Backtracking"},{"text":"Dynamic programming"},{"text":"Greedy algorithms"},{"text":"Sorting"},{"text":"Searching"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Problem-Solving Target"},{"type":"p","text":"Rather than chasing a specific problem count, focus on being able to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Identify patterns"},{"text":"Analyze complexity"},{"text":"Explain trade-offs"},{"text":"Write clean solutions"},{"text":"Test edge cases"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Software Engineering"},{"type":"h","text":"Object-Oriented Design"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Encapsulation"},{"text":"Inheritance"},{"text":"Polymorphism"},{"text":"Abstraction"},{"text":"Interfaces"},{"text":"Composition"},{"text":"Learn commonly used design patterns where they genuinely solve recurring problems."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Database Engineering"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn both relational and non-relational databases."},{"type":"h","text":"SQL"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SELECT"},{"text":"JOINs"},{"text":"GROUP BY"},{"text":"Subqueries"},{"text":"CTEs"},{"text":"Window functions"},{"text":"Indexes"},{"text":"Transactions"},{"text":"Constraints"},{"text":"Normalization"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Databases"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PostgreSQL"},{"text":"MySQL"},{"text":"MongoDB"},{"text":"Redis"},{"text":"Do not just learn CRUD."}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Query optimization"},{"text":"Indexing"},{"text":"Transactions"},{"text":"Isolation"},{"text":"Replication basics"},{"text":"Caching"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Backend Engineering"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose one strong backend ecosystem."},{"type":"h","text":"Java Route"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Java"},{"text":"Spring Boot"},{"text":"Spring MVC"},{"text":"Spring Data JPA"},{"text":"Hibernate"},{"text":"REST APIs"},{"text":"Authentication"},{"text":"Authorization"},{"text":"Validation"},{"text":"Exception handling"},{"text":"API documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Alternative"},{"type":"p","text":"Node.js + TypeScript can also be used, but depth in one backend stack is more valuable than superficial knowledge of several."},{"type":"h","text":"Frontend Engineering"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"HTML"},{"text":"CSS"},{"text":"JavaScript"},{"text":"TypeScript"},{"text":"React"},{"text":"Responsive design"},{"text":"State management"},{"text":"API integration"},{"text":"Form validation"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Performance optimization"},{"text":"Understand how the frontend communicates with backend APIs."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2–3 — Full-Stack Product Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Build applications with:"},{"type":"flow","items":["React / TypeScript","REST / API Layer","Spring Boot / Backend","PostgreSQL","Redis / Cache","Cloud Infrastructure"]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Authentication"},{"text":"Authorization"},{"text":"JWT/session concepts"},{"text":"Role-based access"},{"text":"File uploads"},{"text":"Search"},{"text":"Pagination"},{"text":"Notifications"},{"text":"Background jobs"},{"text":"Rate limiting"},{"text":"Logging"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Software Architecture"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to structure maintainable applications."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Layered architecture"},{"text":"Modular monoliths"},{"text":"Microservices"},{"text":"Event-driven architecture"},{"text":"Service-to-service communication"},{"text":"Message queues"},{"text":"Caching"},{"text":"API gateways"},{"text":"Load balancing"},{"text":"Do not adopt microservices simply because they are popular."},{"text":"For student projects and many early products, a well-designed modular monolith is often the better starting point."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — System Design"},{"type":"p","text":"A Product Engineer must eventually understand how applications behave at scale."},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"h","text":"Scalability"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Horizontal scaling"},{"text":"Vertical scaling"},{"text":"Load balancing"},{"text":"Caching"},{"text":"Database scaling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Reliability"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Redundancy"},{"text":"Failover"},{"text":"Health checks"},{"text":"Retry strategies"},{"text":"Circuit breakers"},{"text":"Graceful degradation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Distributed Systems"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CAP concepts"},{"text":"Consistency"},{"text":"Availability"},{"text":"Partition tolerance"},{"text":"Distributed transactions"},{"text":"Message queues"},{"text":"Eventual consistency"}]},{"type":"h","text":"API Engineering"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"REST"},{"text":"HTTP"},{"text":"JSON"},{"text":"Status codes"},{"text":"API versioning"},{"text":"Pagination"},{"text":"Filtering"},{"text":"Rate limiting"},{"text":"Authentication"},{"text":"Authorization"},{"text":"Also understand when GraphQL, WebSockets or asynchronous messaging may be appropriate."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"Production engineering requires more than manual testing."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"h","text":"Unit Testing"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"JUnit"},{"text":"Mockito"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Integration Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"Test:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"APIs"},{"text":"Database interactions"},{"text":"External services"}]},{"type":"h","text":"End-to-End Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn tools such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Playwright"},{"text":"Cypress"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Engineering Practices"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Test-driven development where useful"},{"text":"Regression testing"},{"text":"CI test automation"},{"text":"Static analysis"},{"text":"Code reviews"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3–4 — Cloud & DevOps"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose one cloud platform deeply."},{"type":"h","text":"AWS"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"EC2"},{"text":"S3"},{"text":"RDS"},{"text":"IAM"},{"text":"VPC fundamentals"},{"text":"CloudWatch"},{"text":"Lambda"},{"text":"ECS/EKS fundamentals"},{"text":"Also understand equivalent services on Azure/GCP conceptually."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Containers"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Docker"},{"text":"Docker images"},{"text":"Containers"},{"text":"Docker Compose"},{"text":"Container networking"},{"text":"Environment configuration"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Then learn Kubernetes fundamentals:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pods"},{"text":"Deployments"},{"text":"Services"},{"text":"ConfigMaps"},{"text":"Secrets"},{"text":"Ingress"},{"text":"You do not need to become a Kubernetes administrator to become a Product Engineer."}]},{"type":"h","text":"CI/CD"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"GitHub Actions"},{"text":"Build pipelines"},{"text":"Automated tests"},{"text":"Deployment pipelines"},{"text":"Environment management"},{"text":"Rollbacks"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Code","Git","Pull Request","Code Review","Automated Tests","Build","Deployment","Monitoring"]},{"type":"h","text":"Observability"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the three major pillars:"},{"type":"h","text":"Logs"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Structured logging"},{"text":"Log levels"},{"text":"Centralized logs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Metrics"},{"type":"p","text":"Monitor:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CPU"},{"text":"Memory"},{"text":"Request rate"},{"text":"Latency"},{"text":"Error rate"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Traces"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Distributed tracing"},{"text":"Request flow"},{"text":"Service dependencies"},{"text":"Learn the importance of SLIs, SLOs and error budgets at a conceptual level."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Product Engineering Mindset"},{"type":"p","text":"This differentiates a Product Engineer from a developer who only implements tickets."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to ask:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Who is using this feature?"},{"text":"What problem does it solve?"},{"text":"How frequently will it be used?"},{"text":"What happens if it fails?"},{"text":"What is the expected performance?"},{"text":"What security risks exist?"},{"text":"How will success be measured?"},{"text":"What happens after deployment?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Product Metrics"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Activation"},{"text":"Conversion"},{"text":"Retention"},{"text":"Engagement"},{"text":"Churn"},{"text":"Feature adoption"},{"text":"Error rate"},{"text":"Performance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"AI & Modern Product Engineering"},{"type":"p","text":"AI is increasingly becoming part of the software product stack."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"h","text":"AI-Assisted Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Use AI tools for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Code exploration"},{"text":"Debugging"},{"text":"Test generation"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Refactoring"},{"text":"Prototyping"},{"text":"But maintain the ability to review, test and validate generated code."}]},{"type":"h","text":"AI Application Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"LLM APIs"},{"text":"Prompt engineering"},{"text":"Embeddings"},{"text":"Vector databases"},{"text":"RAG"},{"text":"Tool/function calling"},{"text":"Evaluation"},{"text":"Guardrails"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A Product Engineer can therefore build:"},{"type":"h","text":"Traditional Software + AI-powered Product Features"},{"type":"h","text":"Security Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"OWASP Top 10"},{"text":"Authentication"},{"text":"Authorization"},{"text":"Password hashing"},{"text":"Session security"},{"text":"Input validation"},{"text":"SQL injection"},{"text":"XSS"},{"text":"CSRF"},{"text":"Secrets management"},{"text":"Dependency vulnerabilities"},{"text":"Secure API design"},{"text":"Security should be considered during design rather than added after development."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Industry-Integrated Learning"},{"type":"p","text":"Since this specialization explicitly includes industry integration, use every industry project to demonstrate real engineering practices."},{"type":"p","text":"For each project, maintain:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Requirements"},{"text":"Architecture diagram"},{"text":"Database schema"},{"text":"API documentation"},{"text":"Git history"},{"text":"Code review"},{"text":"Test suite"},{"text":"CI/CD pipeline"},{"text":"Deployment"},{"text":"Monitoring"},{"text":"Performance measurements"},{"text":"Security considerations"},{"text":"Known limitations"},{"text":"This is much stronger than simply listing project names on a resume."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Final-Year Projects"}]},{"heading":"Production-Grade SaaS Platform","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Build a complete SaaS application with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"React"},{"text":"TypeScript"},{"text":"Spring Boot"},{"text":"PostgreSQL"},{"text":"Redis"},{"text":"Authentication"},{"text":"RBAC"},{"text":"REST APIs"},{"text":"Docker"},{"text":"AWS"},{"text":"CI/CD"},{"text":"Monitoring"},{"text":"Include realistic multi-user workflows and administration."}]}]},{"heading":"AI-Powered Product","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Build an application combining:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"LLM"},{"text":"RAG"},{"text":"Vector database"},{"text":"User authentication"},{"text":"Backend APIs"},{"text":"Evaluation"},{"text":"Observability"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Measure:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Response quality"},{"text":"Latency"},{"text":"Cost"},{"text":"Failure rate"}]}]},{"heading":"High-Scale E-Commerce Backend","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Build services for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Users"},{"text":"Products"},{"text":"Cart"},{"text":"Orders"},{"text":"Payments simulation"},{"text":"Inventory"},{"text":"Search"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Demonstrate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Caching"},{"text":"Transactions"},{"text":"Idempotency"},{"text":"Rate limiting"},{"text":"Asynchronous processing"}]}]},{"heading":"Real-Time Collaboration Application","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Build a system with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"WebSockets"},{"text":"Authentication"},{"text":"Real-time updates"},{"text":"Presence"},{"text":"Notifications"},{"text":"Persistent storage"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Examples:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Collaborative workspace"},{"text":"Team task platform"},{"text":"Real-time dashboard"}]}]},{"heading":"Developer Productivity Platform","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Create an internal developer tool featuring:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Git integration"},{"text":"Automated workflows"},{"text":"CI/CD information"},{"text":"Deployment tracking"},{"text":"Logs"},{"text":"Metrics"},{"text":"AI-assisted troubleshooting"},{"text":"This demonstrates both product thinking and engineering depth."}]}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"h","text":"Product Companies"},{"type":"p","text":"Look for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Software Engineering Intern"},{"text":"Product Engineering Intern"},{"text":"Backend Engineering Intern"},{"text":"Full-Stack Engineering Intern"}]},{"type":"h","text":"SaaS Companies"},{"type":"p","text":"Good exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"APIs"},{"text":"Cloud"},{"text":"Databases"},{"text":"Multi-tenant systems"},{"text":"Product analytics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Startups"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful for learning:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Rapid product development"},{"text":"Full-stack ownership"},{"text":"Deployment"},{"text":"Customer feedback"},{"text":"Feature iteration"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Developer Tools / Platform Companies"},{"type":"p","text":"Excellent for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"APIs"},{"text":"Infrastructure"},{"text":"DevOps"},{"text":"Cloud"},{"text":"Developer experience"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Internship Progression"},{"type":"flow","items":["Year 1","Programming + Git + Small Projects","Year 2","Web / Backend Development Internship","Year 3","Product Engineering / Software Internship","Year 4","Industry Project + Production-Level Internship","Graduate","Product Engineer / Software Engineer"]}]},{"heading":"Entry-Level Career Options","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A graduate can target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Product Engineer"},{"text":"Associate Product Engineer"},{"text":"Software Engineer"},{"text":"Software Development Engineer"},{"text":"Full-Stack Engineer"},{"text":"Backend Engineer"},{"text":"Frontend Engineer"},{"text":"Platform Engineer"},{"text":"Cloud Engineer"},{"text":"DevOps Engineer"},{"text":"Application Engineer"},{"text":"AI Application Engineer"},{"text":"Solutions Engineer"},{"text":"Developer Experience Engineer"},{"text":"The exact title varies considerably across companies."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Employer Skill Matrix"},{"type":"table","header":["Employer Type","Most Valuable Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"SaaS Companies"},{"text":"Full-stack + Cloud + Product Thinking"}],[{"text":"Product Startups"},{"text":"Full-stack + Rapid Development"}],[{"text":"Enterprise Software"},{"text":"Java + Spring + SQL + Cloud"}],[{"text":"FinTech"},{"text":"Backend + Databases + Security"}],[{"text":"E-Commerce"},{"text":"APIs + Distributed Systems + Product Analytics"}],[{"text":"AI Companies"},{"text":"Python + AI/ML + Backend + Cloud"}],[{"text":"Developer Tools"},{"text":"Backend + Cloud + APIs + DevOps"}],[{"text":"Consumer Apps"},{"text":"Frontend + Backend + Product Analytics"}],[{"text":"Platform Teams"},{"text":"Cloud + Distributed Systems + Automation"}]]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Certifications are secondary to demonstrable engineering ability."},{"type":"p","text":"Useful areas:"},{"type":"h","text":"Cloud"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AWS Cloud fundamentals"},{"text":"AWS Developer/Associate-level learning"},{"text":"Azure or GCP equivalents"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Development"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Java/Spring"},{"text":"Web development"},{"text":"Database engineering"}]},{"type":"h","text":"DevOps"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Docker"},{"text":"Kubernetes"},{"text":"CI/CD"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Security"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Application security"},{"text":"Cloud security fundamentals"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong GitHub repository, deployed product and meaningful internship generally provide stronger evidence than a large collection of certificates."}]},{"heading":"PG Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A PG is not mandatory for becoming a Product Engineer."},{"type":"p","text":"M.Tech / M.E."},{"type":"p","text":"Relevant areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Computer Science"},{"text":"Software Engineering"},{"text":"Artificial Intelligence"},{"text":"Data Engineering"},{"text":"Distributed Systems"},{"text":"Information Security"},{"text":"Cloud Computing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"M.S."},{"type":"p","text":"Potential specializations:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Computer Science"},{"text":"Software Engineering"},{"text":"AI"},{"text":"Human-Computer Interaction"},{"text":"Distributed Systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"MBA"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful later for engineers moving toward:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Product Management"},{"text":"Technology Management"},{"text":"Entrepreneurship"},{"text":"Engineering Management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Career Specializations"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Full-Stack Product Engineer"},{"type":"p","text":"Combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["React","TypeScript","Backend","SQL","Cloud"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"2. Backend Product Engineer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"APIs"},{"text":"Databases"},{"text":"Distributed systems"},{"text":"Performance"},{"text":"Reliability"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. AI Product Engineer"},{"type":"p","text":"Combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Software Engineering","LLMs","RAG","AI Infrastructure"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"4. Platform Product Engineer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cloud"},{"text":"Developer platforms"},{"text":"CI/CD"},{"text":"Infrastructure"},{"text":"APIs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5. Data Product Engineer"},{"type":"p","text":"Combine:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Backend"},{"text":"Data pipelines"},{"text":"Analytics"},{"text":"Data products"}]},{"type":"h","text":"6. Mobile Product Engineer"},{"type":"p","text":"Specialize in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Android"},{"text":"iOS"},{"text":"Cross-platform development"}]},{"type":"h","text":"7. Developer Experience Engineer"},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Developer tools"},{"text":"SDKs"},{"text":"APIs"},{"text":"Internal platforms"},{"text":"Automation"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":